@startuml
title What a saga scenario test controls and what it observes

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

component "Scenario test" as T #FFF8E1

package "Under test" #F4F7F9 {
  component "Order service" as O
  component "Inventory service" as I
  component "Payment service" as P
  component "Cart, catalog,\nnotification" as R
}

component "Simulated payment provider\nanswers by token;\nrecords every call" as PSP #E3F2FD
component "Simulated e-mail provider\nrecords every e-mail" as MAIL #E3F2FD
queue "Bus" as BUS
component "Observation subscriptions\none per topic" as OBS #C8E6C9

T --> O : places an order,\ndecides as an administrator
T ..> I : stops and restarts
T ..> P : stops and restarts
T ..> BUS : republishes a message
T ..> PSP : chooses the token
O <--> BUS
I <--> BUS
P <--> BUS
R <-- BUS
P --> PSP
R --> MAIL
BUS --> OBS
T <-- OBS : every message, in order
T <-- PSP : how many charges, cancellations, refunds
T <-- MAIL : which e-mails
T <-- O : status of the order,\nwhat its saga knows

note bottom of T
  Delays are configuration: a scenario
  runs with seconds where production
  has minutes, in the same order.
end note
@enduml
